## tela — capa reactiva ligera para PenguScript/WASM.
##
## Señales explícitas, bindings declarativos `data-tela-*` y reconciliación
## keyed. Sin eval, sin VDOM y sin estado global implícito: las señales se
## registran por nombre y el runtime vive en un singleton de función.

import std.memoria
import std.scrolls
import std.spark
import std.web.dom as dom
import std.web.event as event
import std.web.js as js
import std.web as web

## Identificador estable de una señal o de un observer.
alias Id as u64

## Una celda reactiva. `value` es el valor actual y `subs` los observers que
## la leyeron durante su última ejecución.
rune Cell shard T derive Drop:
    value as T
    subs as list of u64

## Handle de señal. El dueño del handle es la aplicación; para transferirlo al
## registry se usa `register_*`, que libera la celda en `shutdown`.
rune Signal shard T:
    id as u64
    cell as ref to Cell of T

## Handle de efecto. Se libera explícitamente con `dispose_effect`.
rune Effect:
    id as u64

## Dependencia de un observer: permite desuscribirse sin conocer `T`.
rune Dep:
    remove as weave with ctx as ref to void, obs as u64 into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Observer interno del runtime.
rune Observer:
    run as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void
    alive as bool
    dirty as bool
    deps as list of Dep

## Suscripción devuelta por `effect`, `bind_*`, `each` y `when`.
rune Subscription:
    effect_id as u64
    has_cleanup as bool
    cleanup as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Entrada de texto ya formateada. `ctx` apunta a la `Cell<T>` original.
rune TextEntry:
    get as weave with ctx as ref to void into string
    free as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Entrada booleana (show/class/checked).
rune BoolEntry:
    get as weave with ctx as ref to void into bool
    set as weave with ctx as ref to void, v as bool into void
    free as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Entrada de input de texto (two-way).
rune ValueEntry:
    get as weave with ctx as ref to void into string
    set as weave with ctx as ref to void, v as string into void
    free as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Alias público de un handler DOM.
alias Handler as weave with ev as event.Event into void
alias Elem as dom.Element

## Definición type-erased de un `data-tela-each` declarativo.
rune EachEntry:
    run as weave with ctx as ref to void, container as Elem, template as Elem into Subscription
    free as weave with ctx as ref to void into void
    ctx as ref to void

## Grupo de suscripciones con limpieza explícita.
rune ScopeBox:
    subs as list of Subscription

## Handle de scope.
rune Scope:
    id as u64

## Runtime único. Vive en un `static var` de función; no hay `var` de módulo.
rune Runtime:
    next_id as u64
    observers as map of u64 to ref to Observer
    queue as list of u64
    current as u64
    scheduled as bool
    batch_depth as int
    mounted as bool
    mount_subs as list of Subscription
    listeners as list of dom.Listener
    nodes as list of dom.Element
    registered as map of u64 to u64
    text_entries as map of string to TextEntry
    bool_entries as map of string to BoolEntry
    value_entries as map of string to ValueEntry
    handlers as map of string to u64
    each_entries as map of string to EachEntry
    scopes as map of u64 to ref to ScopeBox
    input_bound as bool
    change_bound as bool

weave rt into ref to Runtime:
    static var r as Runtime is with next_id is 1, observers is map of u64 to ref to Observer, queue is list of u64, current is 0, scheduled is false, batch_depth is 0, mounted is false, mount_subs is list of Subscription, listeners is list of dom.Listener, nodes is list of dom.Element, registered is map of u64 to u64, text_entries is map of string to TextEntry, bool_entries is map of string to BoolEntry, value_entries is map of string to ValueEntry, handlers is map of string to u64, each_entries is map of string to EachEntry, scopes is map of u64 to ref to ScopeBox, input_bound is false, change_bound is false
    return sigil of r

weave next_id into u64:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var id as u64 is r->next_id
    set r->next_id is id + 1
    return id

weave panic with message as string into void:
    calling spark.panic with message

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- observers

weave add_observer with run as weave with ctx as ref to void into void, ctx as ref to void into u64:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var id as u64 is calling next_id
    var o as ref to Observer is calling memoria.alloc of Observer
    set o->run is run
    set o->ctx is ctx
    set o->alive is true
    set o->dirty is false
    set o->deps is list of Dep
    calling r->observers.put with id, o
    return id

weave observer_at with id as u64 into ref to Observer:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    return calling r->observers.get with id

## Quita `obs` de la lista de suscriptores de una celda concreta.
weave remove_sub shard T with ctx as ref to void, obs as u64 into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of T is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of T
    var kept as list of u64 is list of u64
    for s in c->subs:
        if s != obs:
            calling kept.push with s
    set c->subs is kept

## Quita `obs` de la lista de suscriptores de una celda concreta.
weave remove_sub shard T with ctx as ref to void, obs as u64 into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of T is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of T
    var kept as list of u64 is list of u64
    for s in c->subs:
        if s != obs:
            calling kept.push with s
    set c->subs is kept

## Limpia las dependencias del observer antes de una nueva ejecución.
weave untrack with o as ref to Observer into void:
    for d in o->deps:
        calling d.remove with d.ctx, 0
    calling o->deps.clear

weave mark_dirty with id as u64 into void:
    var o as ref to Observer is calling observer_at with id
    if not o->alive or o->dirty:
        return
    set o->dirty is true
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    calling r->queue.push with id
    calling schedule

weave run_observer with id as u64 into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->observers.contains with id:
        return
    var o as ref to Observer is calling observer_at with id
    if not o->alive:
        return
    set o->dirty is false
    for d in o->deps:
        calling d.remove with d.ctx, id
    calling o->deps.clear
    set r->current is id
    calling o->run with o->ctx
    set r->current is 0

weave flush into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->batch_depth > 0:
        return
    set r->scheduled is false
    var guard as int is 0
    while r->queue.len > 0:
        set guard is guard + 1
        if guard > 100000:
            calling panic with "tela: dependency cycle in flush"
        var id as u64 is calling r->queue.pop
        calling run_observer with id

weave flush_cb with arg as ref to void into void:
    calling flush

weave schedule into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->scheduled or r->batch_depth > 0:
        return
    set r->scheduled is true
    when wasm:
        calling web.set_timeout with flush_cb, 1.0, null

## Fuerza un flush pendiente. Útil en tests y al final de un handler.
weave flush_now into void:
    calling flush

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- signals

## Registra la celda como dependencia del observer actual (si lo hay).
weave track_cell shard T with c as ref to Cell of T into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->current == 0:
        return
    var already as bool is false
    for s in c->subs:
        if s == r->current:
            set already is true
    if not already:
        calling c->subs.push with r->current
        var o as ref to Observer is calling observer_at with r->current
        calling o->deps.push with (with remove is (remove_sub of T), ctx is (transmute c to ref to void))

## Crea una señal con `initial` y transfiere la celda al llamador.
weave signal shard T with initial as T into Signal of T:
    var c as ref to Cell of T is calling memoria.alloc of Cell of T
    set c->value is initial
    set c->subs is list of u64
    return with id is calling next_id, cell is c

## Lee el valor actual y registra la dependencia si hay un observer activo.
## Escritura concreta para `Signal<int>` (evita una especialización errónea
## del método genérico cuando se llama desde un handler de evento).
weave set_int with s as (Signal of int), v as int into void:
    set s.cell->value is v
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    for id in s.cell->subs:
        calling mark_dirty with id
    calling schedule

## Escritura concreta para `Signal<bool>`.
weave set_bool with s as (Signal of bool), v as bool into void:
    set s.cell->value is v
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    for id in s.cell->subs:
        calling mark_dirty with id
    calling schedule

enchanting Signal shard T:
    weave get into T:
        calling track_cell of T with self->cell
        return self->cell->value

    ## Escribe el valor y marca a los suscriptores.
    weave set with v as T into void:
        set self->cell->value is v
        for sub in self->cell->subs:
            calling mark_dirty with sub
        calling schedule

    ## Aplica una función pura al valor actual.
    weave update with f as weave with v as T into T into void:
        var current as T is calling self.get
        calling self.set with (calling f with current)

    ## Libera la celda. No debe llamarse si la señal fue registrada.
    weave dispose into void:
        var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
        if calling r->registered.contains with self->id:
            calling panic with "tela: cannot dispose a registered signal"
        banish self->cell

## Efecto que corre `run` ya y se re-ejecuta al cambiar sus dependencias.
weave effect with run as weave with ctx as ref to void into void, ctx as ref to void into Effect:
    var id as u64 is calling add_observer with run, ctx
    calling run_observer with id
    return with id is id

## Igual que `effect`, con contexto explícito.
weave effect_with with run as weave with ctx as ref to void into void, ctx as ref to void into Effect:
    return calling effect with run, ctx

weave dispose_effect with e as Effect into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->observers.contains with e.id:
        return
    var o as ref to Observer is calling observer_at with e.id
    set o->alive is false
    for d in o->deps:
        calling d.remove with d.ctx, e.id
    calling o->deps.clear
    calling r->observers.remove with e.id
    banish o

## Deshace una suscripción: mata el efecto y ejecuta su cleanup.
enchanting Subscription:
    weave dispose into void:
        if self->effect_id != 0:
            calling dispose_effect with (with id is self->effect_id)
        if self->has_cleanup:
            calling self->cleanup with self->ctx
        set self->has_cleanup is false
        set self->effect_id is 0

## Agrupa escrituras: el flush ocurre al salir del bloque.
weave batch with work as weave into void into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    set r->batch_depth is r->batch_depth + 1
    calling work
    set r->batch_depth is r->batch_depth - 1
    if r->batch_depth == 0:
        calling flush

## Versión con contexto para no capturar.
weave batch_with with work as weave with ctx as ref to void into void, ctx as ref to void into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    set r->batch_depth is r->batch_depth + 1
    calling work with ctx
    set r->batch_depth is r->batch_depth - 1
    if r->batch_depth == 0:
        calling flush

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ derived

rune Derived shard A, B:
    source as ref to Cell of A
    f as weave with a as A into B
    value as B

## Derivada de una señal con una función pura `A -> B`.
weave derived1 shard A, B with f as (weave with a as A into B), src as Signal of A into Derived of A, B:
    return with source is src.cell, f is f, value is (calling f with src.cell->value)

enchanting Derived shard A, B:
    weave get into B:
        calling track_cell of A with self->source
        set self->value is calling self->f with self->source->value
        return self->value

    weave dispose into void:
        banish self

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- registry

weave text_of_string with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of string is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of string
    calling track_cell of string with c
    return c->value

weave text_of_int with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of int is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of int
    calling track_cell of int with c
    return calling spark.str_int with c->value

weave text_of_float with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of float is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of float
    calling track_cell of float with c
    return calling spark.str_float with c->value

weave text_of_bool_text with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of bool is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of bool
    calling track_cell of bool with c
    return calling spark.str_bool with c->value

weave bool_of_bool with ctx as ref to void into bool:
    var c as ref to Cell of bool is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of bool
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->current != 0:
        var already as bool is false
        for s in c->subs:
            if s == r->current:
                set already is true
        if not already:
            calling c->subs.push with r->current
    return c->value

weave free_string_cell with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of string is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of string
    banish c

weave free_int_cell with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of int is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of int
    banish c

weave free_float_cell with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of float is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of float
    banish c

weave free_bool_cell with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of bool is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of bool
    banish c

weave register_text with name as string, s as Signal of string into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->text_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate signal name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->text_entries.put with name, e

weave register_int with name as string, s as Signal of int into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->text_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate signal name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_int, free is free_int_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->text_entries.put with name, e

weave register_float with name as string, s as Signal of float into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->text_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate signal name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_float, free is free_float_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->text_entries.put with name, e

weave register_bool_text with name as string, s as Signal of bool into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->text_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate signal name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_bool_text, free is free_bool_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->text_entries.put with name, e

weave register_bool with name as string, s as Signal of bool into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->bool_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate bool name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as BoolEntry is with get is bool_of_bool, set is bool_set_bool, free is free_bool_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->bool_entries.put with name, e

weave get_text with name as string into TextEntry:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->text_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: unknown text signal: " + name
    return calling r->text_entries.get with name

weave get_bool with name as string into BoolEntry:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->bool_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: unknown bool signal: " + name
    return calling r->bool_entries.get with name

weave register_handler with name as string, h as Handler into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->handlers.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate handler name: " + name
    calling r->handlers.put with name, (transmute h to u64)

weave handler_index with name as string into int:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->handlers.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: unknown handler: " + name
    return 0

weave free_all_entries into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    for k, e in r->text_entries:
        calling e.free with e.ctx
    for k, e in r->bool_entries:
        calling e.free with e.ctx
    for k, e in r->value_entries:
        calling e.free with e.ctx
    for k, e in r->each_entries:
        calling e.free with e.ctx
    calling r->text_entries.clear
    calling r->bool_entries.clear
    calling r->value_entries.clear
    calling r->each_entries.clear
    calling r->handlers.clear

## Libera registry, bindings y observers. La app no debe usar tela después.
weave shutdown into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    calling unmount
    for id, o in r->observers:
        var op as ref to Observer is o
        set op->alive is false
        banish op
    calling r->observers.clear
    calling r->queue.clear
    calling free_all_entries
    calling r->registered.clear

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ bindings

rune TextBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    entry as TextEntry
    owns as bool

rune BoolBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    entry as BoolEntry
    owns as bool

rune ClassBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    name as string
    entry as BoolEntry
    owns as bool

rune AttrBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    name as string
    entry as TextEntry
    owns as bool

rune StyleBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    prop as string
    entry as TextEntry
    owns as bool

rune HtmlBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    entry as TextEntry
    owns as bool

rune ValueBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    entry as ValueEntry

rune CheckedBinding:
    node as dom.Element
    entry as BoolEntry

weave text_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to TextBinding is transmute ctx to ref to TextBinding
    var v as string is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    calling dom.set_text with b->node, v

weave bool_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to BoolBinding is transmute ctx to ref to BoolBinding
    var v as bool is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    if v:
        calling dom.remove_attr with b->node, "hidden"
    else:
        calling dom.set_attr with b->node, "hidden", "hidden"

weave class_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to ClassBinding is transmute ctx to ref to ClassBinding
    var v as bool is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    if v:
        calling dom.add_class with b->node, b->name
    else:
        calling dom.remove_class with b->node, b->name

weave attr_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to AttrBinding is transmute ctx to ref to AttrBinding
    var v as string is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    calling dom.set_attr with b->node, b->name, v

weave style_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to StyleBinding is transmute ctx to ref to StyleBinding
    var v as string is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    calling dom.set_style with b->node, b->prop, v

weave html_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to HtmlBinding is transmute ctx to ref to HtmlBinding
    var v as string is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    calling dom.set_html_unsafe with b->node, v

weave value_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to ValueBinding is transmute ctx to ref to ValueBinding
    var v as string is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    calling dom.set_value with b->node, v

weave free_text_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to TextBinding is transmute ctx to ref to TextBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave free_bool_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to BoolBinding is transmute ctx to ref to BoolBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave free_class_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to ClassBinding is transmute ctx to ref to ClassBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave free_attr_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to AttrBinding is transmute ctx to ref to AttrBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave free_style_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to StyleBinding is transmute ctx to ref to StyleBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave free_html_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to HtmlBinding is transmute ctx to ref to HtmlBinding
    if b->owns:
        calling b->entry.free with b->entry.ctx
    banish b

weave make_sub with effect_id as u64, cleanup as (weave with ctx as ref to void into void), ctx as ref to void into Subscription:
    return with effect_id is effect_id, has_cleanup is true, cleanup is cleanup, ctx is ctx

weave text_entry_of with name as string into TextEntry:
    return calling get_text with name

weave bool_entry_of with name as string into BoolEntry:
    return calling get_bool with name

weave bind_text_entry with node as dom.Element, e as TextEntry, owns as bool into Subscription:
    var b as ref to TextBinding is calling memoria.alloc of TextBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is owns
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with text_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_text_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave bind_bool_entry with node as dom.Element, e as BoolEntry, owns as bool into Subscription:
    var b as ref to BoolBinding is calling memoria.alloc of BoolBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is owns
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with bool_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_bool_binding, transmute b to ref to void

## Bindea `node.textContent` a una señal de string. Transfiere la señal.
weave bind_text with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of string into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    return calling bind_text_entry with node, e, true

## Bindea `textContent` a una señal int ya formateada.
weave bind_int with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of int into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_int, free is free_int_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    return calling bind_text_entry with node, e, true

## Bindea `textContent` a una señal float ya formateada.
weave bind_float with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of float into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_float, free is free_float_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    return calling bind_text_entry with node, e, true

## Bindea `textContent` a una señal bool ya formateada.
weave bind_bool_text with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of bool into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_bool_text, free is free_bool_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    return calling bind_text_entry with node, e, true

## Bindea el atributo `hidden` a una señal bool.
weave bind_show with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of bool into Subscription:
    var e as BoolEntry is with get is bool_of_bool, set is bool_set_bool, free is free_bool_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    return calling bind_bool_entry with node, e, true

## Bindea una clase a una señal bool.
weave bind_class with node as dom.Element, name as string, s as Signal of bool into Subscription:
    var e as BoolEntry is with get is bool_of_bool, set is bool_set_bool, free is free_bool_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    var b as ref to ClassBinding is calling memoria.alloc of ClassBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->name is name
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is true
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with class_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_class_binding, transmute b to ref to void

## Bindea un atributo a una señal de string.
weave bind_attr with node as dom.Element, name as string, s as Signal of string into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    var b as ref to AttrBinding is calling memoria.alloc of AttrBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->name is name
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is true
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with attr_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_attr_binding, transmute b to ref to void

## Bindea una propiedad CSS a una señal de string.
weave bind_style with node as dom.Element, prop as string, s as Signal of string into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    var b as ref to StyleBinding is calling memoria.alloc of StyleBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->prop is prop
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is true
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with style_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_style_binding, transmute b to ref to void

## Bindea `innerHTML` sin escapar. El nombre lo dice: es una escotilla XSS.
weave bind_html_unsafe with node as dom.Element, s as Signal of string into Subscription:
    var e as TextEntry is with get is text_of_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    var b as ref to HtmlBinding is calling memoria.alloc of HtmlBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is true
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with html_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_html_binding, transmute b to ref to void

# --------------------------------------------------------------- two-way DOM

weave value_get_string with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of string is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of string
    calling track_cell of string with c
    return c->value

weave value_set_string with ctx as ref to void, v as string into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of string is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of string
    set c->value is v
    for sub in c->subs:
        calling mark_dirty with sub
    calling schedule

weave bool_set_bool with ctx as ref to void, v as bool into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of bool is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of bool
    set c->value is v
    for sub in c->subs:
        calling mark_dirty with sub
    calling schedule

weave value_get_int with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of int is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of int
    calling track_cell of int with c
    return calling spark.str_int with c->value

weave value_set_int with ctx as ref to void, v as string into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of int is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of int
    var parsed as int is (calling spark.parse_int with v) or else c->value
    if parsed != c->value:
        set c->value is parsed
        for sub in c->subs:
            calling mark_dirty with sub
        calling schedule

weave value_get_float with ctx as ref to void into string:
    var c as ref to Cell of float is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of float
    calling track_cell of float with c
    return calling spark.str_float with c->value

weave value_set_float with ctx as ref to void, v as string into void:
    var c as ref to Cell of float is transmute ctx to ref to Cell of float
    var parsed as float is (calling spark.parse_float with v) or else c->value
    if parsed != c->value:
        set c->value is parsed
        for sub in c->subs:
            calling mark_dirty with sub
        calling schedule

weave register_value_int with name as string, s as Signal of int into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->value_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate value name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as ValueEntry is with get is value_get_int, set is value_set_int, free is free_int_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->value_entries.put with name, e

weave register_value_float with name as string, s as Signal of float into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->value_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate value name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as ValueEntry is with get is value_get_float, set is value_set_float, free is free_float_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->value_entries.put with name, e

weave register_value with name as string, s as Signal of string into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->value_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate value name: " + name
    if calling r->registered.contains with s.id:
        calling panic with "tela: signal already registered"
    calling r->registered.put with s.id, s.id
    var e as ValueEntry is with get is value_get_string, set is value_set_string, free is free_string_cell, ctx is transmute s.cell to ref to void
    calling r->value_entries.put with name, e

weave get_value with name as string into ValueEntry:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->value_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: unknown value signal: " + name
    return calling r->value_entries.get with name

weave checked_binding_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to CheckedBinding is transmute ctx to ref to CheckedBinding
    var v as bool is calling b->entry.get with b->entry.ctx
    var r as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.set_checked with b->node, v

weave free_checked_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to CheckedBinding is transmute ctx to ref to CheckedBinding
    banish b

weave bind_checked_entry with node as dom.Element, e as BoolEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to CheckedBinding is calling memoria.alloc of CheckedBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with checked_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_checked_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave bind_value_entry with node as dom.Element, e as ValueEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to ValueBinding is calling memoria.alloc of ValueBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with value_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_value_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave free_value_binding with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var b as ref to ValueBinding is transmute ctx to ref to ValueBinding
    banish b

## Bindea un input two-way por nombre registrado con `register_value`.
weave bind_value with node as dom.Element, name as string into Subscription:
    return calling bind_value_entry with node, (calling get_value with name)

weave bind_checked with node as dom.Element, name as string into Subscription:
    var e as BoolEntry is calling get_bool with name
    return calling bind_checked_entry with node, e

weave on_input with ev as event.Event into void:
    var tr as result of js.JsValue to js.JsError is calling event.target with ev
    if not tr.is_ok:
        return
    var tv as js.JsValue is tr.value
    var er as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.wrap with tv
    if not er.is_ok:
        return
    var el as dom.Element is er.value
    var nr as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.get_attr with el, "data-tela-value"
    if not nr.is_ok:
        calling dom.free with (sigil of el)
        return
    if nr.value is present:
        var name as string is nr.value.value
        var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
        if calling r->value_entries.contains with name:
            var e as ValueEntry is calling get_value with name
            var vr as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.value with el
            if vr.is_ok and vr.value is present:
                var sv as string is vr.value.value
                calling e.set with e.ctx, sv
    calling dom.free with (sigil of el)
    calling flush

weave on_change with ev as event.Event into void:
    var tr as result of js.JsValue to js.JsError is calling event.target with ev
    if not tr.is_ok:
        return
    var er as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.wrap with tr.value
    if not er.is_ok:
        return
    var el as dom.Element is er.value
    var nr as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.get_attr with el, "data-tela-checked"
    if nr.is_ok and nr.value is present:
        var name as string is nr.value.value
        var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
        if calling r->bool_entries.contains with name:
            var e as BoolEntry is calling get_bool with name
            var cv as bool is calling dom.checked with el
            calling e.set with e.ctx, cv
    calling dom.free with (sigil of el)

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- mount
    calling flush

weave attr_value with node as dom.Element, name as string into string:
    var r as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.get_attr with node, name
    if not r.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot read attribute " + name
    if r.value is present:
        return r.value.value
    return ""

weave add_listener with node as dom.Element, kind as string, h as Handler into void:
    var r as result of dom.Listener to js.JsError is calling dom.on with node, kind, h
    if not r.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot listen to " + kind
    var rt0 as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    calling rt0->listeners.push with r.value

weave call_handler with name as string, ev as event.Event into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var addr as u64 is calling r->handlers.get with name
    var h as Handler is transmute addr to Handler
    calling h with ev

weave dispatch_event with ev as event.Event into void:
    var tr as result of js.JsValue to js.JsError is calling event.target with ev
    if not tr.is_ok:
        return
    var er as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.wrap with tr.value
    if not er.is_ok:
        return
    var kr as result of string to js.JsError is calling event.kind with ev
    if not kr.is_ok:
        calling dom.free with (sigil of er.value)
        return
    var sel as string is "[data-tela-on-" + kr.value + "]"
    var cr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.closest with er.value, sel
    calling dom.free with (sigil of er.value)
    if not cr.is_ok or cr.value is not present:
        return
    var host as dom.Element is cr.value.value
    var an as string is "data-tela-on-" + kr.value
    var ar as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.get_attr with host, an
    if ar.is_ok and ar.value is present:
        calling call_handler with ar.value.value, ev
        calling flush
    calling dom.free with (sigil of host)

weave bind_attr_entry with node as dom.Element, name as string, e as TextEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to AttrBinding is calling memoria.alloc of AttrBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->name is name
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is false
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with attr_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_attr_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave bind_class_entry with node as dom.Element, name as string, e as BoolEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to ClassBinding is calling memoria.alloc of ClassBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->name is name
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is false
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with class_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_class_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave bind_style_entry with node as dom.Element, prop as string, e as TextEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to StyleBinding is calling memoria.alloc of StyleBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->prop is prop
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is false
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with style_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_style_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave bind_html_entry with node as dom.Element, e as TextEntry into Subscription:
    var b as ref to HtmlBinding is calling memoria.alloc of HtmlBinding
    set b->node is node
    set b->entry is e
    set b->owns is false
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with html_binding_run, transmute b to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_html_binding, transmute b to ref to void

weave mount_add with sub as Subscription into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    calling r->mount_subs.push with sub

rune IfState:
    anchor as dom.Element
    template as dom.Element
    cond as ref to Cell of bool
    has_current as bool
    current as maybe dom.Element
    current_value as bool
    visible as bool
    rebuild as bool
    subs as list of Subscription

weave if_track with st as ref to IfState into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->current == 0:
        return
    var already as bool is false
    for s in st->cond->subs:
        if s == r->current:
            set already is true
    if not already:
        calling st->cond->subs.push with r->current
        var o as ref to Observer is calling observer_at with r->current
        calling o->deps.push with (with remove is (remove_sub of bool), ctx is (transmute st->cond to ref to void))

weave if_dispose with st as ref to IfState into void:
    for sub in st->subs:
        calling sub.dispose
    calling st->subs.clear
    if st->has_current and st->current is present:
        var old as dom.Element is st->current.value
        if st->visible:
            var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with old
        calling dom.free with (sigil of old)
    set st->has_current is false
    set st->current is maybe none
    set st->visible is false

weave if_insert with st as ref to IfState, node as dom.Element into void:
    var pr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.parent with st->anchor
    if not pr.is_ok or pr.value is not present:
        calling panic with "tela: data-tela-if has no parent"
    var par as dom.Element is pr.value.value
    var ir as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.insert_before with par, node, (some st->anchor)
    calling dom.free with (sigil of par)
    if not ir.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: data-tela-if insert failed"

weave if_build with st as ref to IfState into void:
    var cr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.clone with st->template
    if not cr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: data-tela-if clone failed"
    var node as dom.Element is cr.value
    calling dom.remove_attr with node, "data-tela-if"
    calling dom.remove_attr with node, "data-tela-if-mode"
    calling if_insert with st, node
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var start as int is r->mount_subs.len
    calling apply_tree with node
    while r->mount_subs.len > start:
        var sub as Subscription is (r->mount_subs at start)
        calling st->subs.push with sub
        calling r->mount_subs.pop
    set st->current is some node
    set st->has_current is true
    set st->visible is true

weave if_show with st as ref to IfState into void:
    if not st->has_current:
        calling if_build with st
        return
    if st->visible:
        return
    if st->current is present:
        calling if_insert with st, st->current.value
        set st->visible is true

weave if_hide with st as ref to IfState into void:
    if not st->visible or not st->has_current:
        return
    if st->current is present:
        var old as dom.Element is st->current.value
        var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with old
    set st->visible is false

weave if_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to IfState is transmute ctx to ref to IfState
    calling if_track with st
    var v as bool is st->cond->value
    if not st->has_current:
        if not v:
            set st->current_value is false
            return
        calling if_build with st
        set st->current_value is true
        return
    if v == st->current_value:
        return
    if v:
        if st->rebuild:
            calling if_dispose with st
        calling if_show with st
    else:
        if st->rebuild:
            calling if_dispose with st
        else:
            calling if_hide with st
    set st->current_value is v

weave free_if with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to IfState is transmute ctx to ref to IfState
    calling if_dispose with st
    calling dom.free with (sigil of st->template)
    banish st

weave mount_if with node as dom.Element, name as string into void:
    var cr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.create_comment with "tela-if"
    if not cr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot create if anchor"
    var anchor as dom.Element is cr.value
    var pr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.parent with node
    if not pr.is_ok or pr.value is not present:
        calling panic with "tela: data-tela-if node has no parent"
    var par as dom.Element is pr.value.value
    var ir as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.insert_before with par, anchor, (some node)
    calling dom.free with (sigil of par)
    if not ir.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot place if anchor"
    var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with node
    if not rr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot detach if template"
    var st as ref to IfState is calling memoria.alloc of IfState
    var ce as BoolEntry is calling get_bool with name
    set st->anchor is anchor
    set st->template is node
    set st->cond is transmute ce.ctx to ref to Cell of bool
    set st->has_current is false
    set st->current is maybe none
    set st->current_value is false
    set st->visible is false
    var mr as result of maybe string to js.JsError is calling dom.get_attr with node, "data-tela-if-mode"
    set st->rebuild is false
    if mr.is_ok and mr.value is present:
        if mr.value.value == "rebuild":
            set st->rebuild is true
    set st->subs is list of Subscription
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with if_run, transmute st to ref to void
    calling mount_add with (calling make_sub with ef.id, free_if, transmute st to ref to void)

weave apply_attr with node as dom.Element, attr as string into void:
    if attr == "data-tela-text":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_text_entry with node, (calling get_text with name), false)
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-html-unsafe":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_html_entry with node, (calling get_text with name))
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-show":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_bool_entry with node, (calling get_bool with name), false)
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-value" or attr == "data-tela-value-int" or attr == "data-tela-value-float":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_value_entry with node, (calling get_value with name))
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-checked":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_checked_entry with node, (calling get_bool with name))
        return
    if calling scrolls.starts_with with attr, "data-tela-attr-":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        var field as string is calling attr.get_substring with 15, attr.len
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_attr_entry with node, field, (calling get_text with name))
        return
    if calling scrolls.starts_with with attr, "data-tela-class-":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        var field as string is calling attr.get_substring with 16, attr.len
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_class_entry with node, field, (calling get_bool with name))
        return
    if calling scrolls.starts_with with attr, "data-tela-style-":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        var field as string is calling attr.get_substring with 16, attr.len
        calling mount_add with (calling bind_style_entry with node, field, (calling get_text with name))
        return
    if calling scrolls.starts_with with attr, "data-tela-on-":
        var kind as string is calling attr.get_substring with 13, attr.len
        if kind != "click" and kind != "input" and kind != "change" and kind != "keydown" and kind != "submit":
            var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
            calling add_listener with node, kind, dispatch_event
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-if":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_if with node, name
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-if-mode":
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-each":
        var name as string is calling attr_value with node, attr
        calling mount_each with node, name
        return
    if attr == "data-tela-key":
        return
    calling panic with "tela: unknown attribute " + attr

weave apply_node with node as dom.Element into void:
    var r as result of list of string to js.JsError is calling dom.attribute_names with node
    if not r.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot read attributes"
    for attr in r.value:
        if calling scrolls.starts_with with attr, "data-tela-":
            calling apply_attr with node, attr
    banish r.value

weave apply_tree with node as dom.Element into void:
    calling apply_node with node
    var ar as result of list of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.query_all_under with node, "*"
    if ar.is_ok:
        for child in ar.value:
            calling apply_node with child
        banish ar.value

weave install_global_listeners into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not r->input_bound:
        var dr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.document
        if dr.is_ok:
            calling add_listener with dr.value, "input", on_input
        set r->input_bound is true
    if not r->change_bound:
        var dr2 as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.document
        if dr2.is_ok:
            calling add_listener with dr2.value, "change", on_change
        set r->change_bound is true
    var dr3 as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.document
    if dr3.is_ok:
        calling add_listener with dr3.value, "click", dispatch_event
        calling add_listener with dr3.value, "keydown", dispatch_event
        calling add_listener with dr3.value, "submit", dispatch_event
        calling add_listener with dr3.value, "input", dispatch_event
        calling add_listener with dr3.value, "change", dispatch_event

## Escanea `root_selector`, conecta los `data-tela-*` y los registra.
weave mount with root_selector as string into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->mounted:
        calling panic with "tela: already mounted"
    var qr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.query_required with root_selector
    if not qr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: mount root not found: " + root_selector
    var root as dom.Element is qr.value
    calling r->nodes.push with root
    calling apply_node with root
    var allr as result of list of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.query_all_under with root, "*"
    if allr.is_ok:
        for node in allr.value:
            if calling dom.is_connected with node:
                calling r->nodes.push with node
                calling apply_node with node
    calling install_global_listeners
    set r->mounted is true

## Libera bindings, listeners y efectos creados por `mount`.
weave unmount into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    for s in r->mount_subs:
        calling s.dispose
    calling r->mount_subs.clear
    var li as int is 0
    while li < r->listeners.len:
        var lv as dom.Listener is (r->listeners at li)
        calling dom.free_listener with (sigil of lv)
        set li is li + 1
    calling r->listeners.clear
    var ni as int is 0
    while ni < r->nodes.len:
        var nv as dom.Element is (r->nodes at ni)
        calling dom.free with (sigil of nv)
        set ni is ni + 1
    calling r->nodes.clear
    set r->mounted is false
    set r->input_bound is false
    set r->change_bound is false

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- each

rune EachState shard T:
    container as dom.Element
    source as ref to Cell of list of T
    key_fn as weave with item as ref to T into string
    render_fn as weave with item as ref to T into Elem
    update_fn as weave with item as ref to T, node as Elem into void
    keys as list of string
    nodes as map of string to dom.Element
    items as list of T

weave each_run shard T with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to EachState of T is transmute ctx to ref to EachState of T
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->current != 0:
        var already as bool is false
        for s in st->source->subs:
            if s == r->current:
                set already is true
        if not already:
            calling st->source->subs.push with r->current
    var items as list of T is st->source->value
    var new_keys as list of string is list of string
    var new_nodes as map of string to dom.Element is map of string to dom.Element
    for item in items:
        var key as string is calling st->key_fn with sigil of item
        calling new_keys.push with key
        if calling st->nodes.contains with key:
            var node as dom.Element is calling st->nodes.get with key
            calling st->update_fn with sigil of item, node
            calling new_nodes.put with key, node
        else:
            var node2 as dom.Element is calling st->render_fn with sigil of item
            var ar as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.append with st->container, node2
            if not ar.is_ok:
                calling panic with "tela: each append failed"
            calling new_nodes.put with key, node2
    for k in st->keys:
        if not calling new_nodes.contains with k:
            var old as dom.Element is calling st->nodes.get with k
            var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with old
            calling dom.free with (sigil of old)
    for k in new_keys:
        var node3 as dom.Element is calling new_nodes.get with k
        var ar2 as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.append with st->container, node3
        if not ar2.is_ok:
            calling panic with "tela: each reorder failed"
    set st->keys is new_keys
    set st->nodes is new_nodes

weave free_each shard T with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to EachState of T is transmute ctx to ref to EachState of T
    for k in st->keys:
        var node as dom.Element is calling st->nodes.get with k
        var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with node
        calling dom.free with (sigil of node)
    banish st

weave ensure_each shard T with st as ref to EachState of T into void:
    return

## Renderiza una lista keyed. `update_fn` recibe el item y el nodo existente.
weave each shard T with key_fn as (weave with item as ref to T into string), render_fn as (weave with item as ref to T into Elem), update_fn as (weave with item as ref to T, node as Elem into void), container as dom.Element, source as Signal of list of T into Subscription:
    var st as ref to EachState of T is calling memoria.alloc of EachState of T
    calling ensure_each of T with st
    set st->container is container
    set st->source is source.cell
    set st->key_fn is key_fn
    set st->render_fn is render_fn
    set st->update_fn is update_fn
    set st->keys is list of string
    set st->nodes is map of string to dom.Element
    set st->items is list of T
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with (each_run of T), transmute st to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, (free_each of T), transmute st to ref to void

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- when

rune WhenState:
    container as dom.Element
    cond as ref to Cell of bool
    then_fn as weave with dummy as int into Elem
    else_fn as weave with dummy as int into Elem
    current as maybe dom.Element
    has_current as bool
    current_value as bool

weave when_run with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to WhenState is transmute ctx to ref to WhenState
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if r->current != 0:
        var already as bool is false
        for s in st->cond->subs:
            if s == r->current:
                set already is true
        if not already:
            calling st->cond->subs.push with r->current
    var v as bool is st->cond->value
    if st->has_current and v == st->current_value:
        return
    if st->has_current:
        if st->current is present:
            var old as dom.Element is st->current.value
            var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with old
            calling dom.free with (sigil of old)
    var node as dom.Element is calling st->then_fn with 0
    if not v:
        set node is calling st->else_fn with 0
    var ar as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.append with st->container, node
    if not ar.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: when append failed"
    set st->current is some node
    set st->has_current is true
    set st->current_value is v

weave free_when with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to WhenState is transmute ctx to ref to WhenState
    if st->has_current and st->current is present:
        var old as dom.Element is st->current.value
        var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with old
        calling dom.free with (sigil of old)
    banish st

## Condicional estructural. `then_fn`/`else_fn` no capturan; usan señales propias.
weave conditional with then_fn as (weave with dummy as int into Elem), else_fn as (weave with dummy as int into Elem), container as dom.Element, cond as Signal of bool into Subscription:
    var st as ref to WhenState is calling memoria.alloc of WhenState
    set st->container is container
    set st->cond is cond.cell
    set st->then_fn is then_fn
    set st->else_fn is else_fn
    set st->current is maybe none
    set st->has_current is false
    set st->current_value is false
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with when_run, transmute st to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, free_when, transmute st to ref to void

# ------------------------------------------------- declarative each (0.2)

## Configuración type-erased de un `data-tela-each`.
rune TplConfig shard T:
    source as ref to Cell of list of T
    key_fn as weave with item as ref to T into string
    bind_fn as weave with item as ref to T, node as Elem into void

## Una fila renderizada desde una plantilla.
rune TplRow:
    key as string
    node as Elem
    subs as list of Subscription

## Estado de una instancia montada de `data-tela-each`.
rune TplState shard T:
    anchor as Elem
    template as Elem
    owned as list of Elem
    config as ref to TplConfig of T
    rows as map of string to ref to TplRow
    keys as list of string

## Recoge las suscripciones creadas por `apply_tree` desde `start`.
weave collect_subs with start as int into list of Subscription:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var out as list of Subscription is list of Subscription
    while r->mount_subs.len > start:
        var sub as Subscription is (r->mount_subs at start)
        calling out.push with sub
        calling r->mount_subs.pop
    return out

## Libera una fila: suscripciones, nodo del DOM y handle.
weave free_tpl_row with row as ref to TplRow into void:
    for sub in row->subs:
        calling sub.dispose
    calling row->subs.clear
    var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with row->node
    calling dom.free with (sigil of row->node)
    banish row

weave tpl_run shard T with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to TplState of T is transmute ctx to ref to TplState of T
    var cfg as ref to TplConfig of T is st->config
    calling track_cell of (list of T) with cfg->source
    var pr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.parent with st->anchor
    if not pr.is_ok or pr.value is not present:
        calling panic with "tela: each anchor has no parent"
    var parent as dom.Element is pr.value.value
    var items as list of T is cfg->source->value
    var new_keys as list of string is list of string
    for item in items:
        var key as string is calling cfg->key_fn with sigil of item
        calling new_keys.push with key
        if calling st->rows.contains with key:
            var row as ref to TplRow is calling st->rows.get with key
            for sub in row->subs:
                calling sub.dispose
            calling row->subs.clear
            var start as int is (calling rt)->mount_subs.len
            calling apply_tree with row->node
            set row->subs is calling collect_subs with start
            calling cfg->bind_fn with sigil of item, row->node
        else:
            var cr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.clone with st->template
            if not cr.is_ok:
                calling panic with "tela: data-tela-each clone failed"
            var node as dom.Element is cr.value
            calling dom.remove_attr with node, "data-tela-each"
            calling dom.remove_attr with node, "data-tela-key"
            var ir as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.insert_before with parent, node, (some st->anchor)
            if not ir.is_ok:
                calling panic with "tela: data-tela-each insert failed"
            var start2 as int is (calling rt)->mount_subs.len
            calling apply_tree with node
            var subs as list of Subscription is calling collect_subs with start2
            calling cfg->bind_fn with sigil of item, node
            var row2 as ref to TplRow is calling memoria.alloc of TplRow
            set row2->key is key
            set row2->node is node
            set row2->subs is subs
            calling st->rows.put with key, row2
    var kept as list of string is list of string
    for k in st->keys:
        if not (calling contains_string with new_keys, k):
            var old as ref to TplRow is calling st->rows.get with k
            calling free_tpl_row with old
            calling st->rows.remove with k
        else:
            calling kept.push with k
    for k in new_keys:
        var row3 as ref to TplRow is calling st->rows.get with k
        var ir2 as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.insert_before with parent, row3->node, (some st->anchor)
        if not ir2.is_ok:
            calling panic with "tela: data-tela-each reorder failed"
    set st->keys is new_keys
    calling dom.free with (sigil of parent)

weave contains_string with items as list of string, value as string into bool:
    for it in items:
        if it == value:
            return true
    return false

weave free_tpl_state shard T with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var st as ref to TplState of T is transmute ctx to ref to TplState of T
    for k in st->keys:
        if calling st->rows.contains with k:
            var row as ref to TplRow is calling st->rows.get with k
            calling free_tpl_row with row
    var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with st->anchor
    calling dom.free with (sigil of st->anchor)
    var oi as int is 0
    while oi < st->owned.len:
        var oe as dom.Element is (st->owned at oi)
        calling dom.free with (sigil of oe)
        set oi is oi + 1
    calling st->owned.clear
    banish st

weave children_of with e as dom.Element into list of dom.Element:
    var r as result of list of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.children with e
    if not r.is_ok:
        return list of dom.Element
    return r.value

weave tpl_start shard T with ctx as ref to void, container as Elem, template as Elem into Subscription:
    var cfg as ref to TplConfig of T is transmute ctx to ref to TplConfig of T
    var cr as result of dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.create_comment with "tela-each"
    if not cr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot create each anchor"
    var st as ref to TplState of T is calling memoria.alloc of TplState of T
    set st->anchor is cr.value
    set st->template is template
    set st->owned is list of Elem
    calling st->owned.push with template
    set st->config is cfg
    set st->rows is map of string to ref to TplRow
    set st->keys is list of string
    var tcr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.template_content with template
    if tcr.is_ok and tcr.value is present:
        var frag as dom.Element is tcr.value.value
        calling st->owned.push with frag
        var kids as list of dom.Element is calling children_of with frag
        if kids.len > 0:
            var first as dom.Element is (kids at 0)
            set st->template is first
            calling st->owned.push with first
        banish kids
    var ir as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.insert_before with container, st->anchor, (some template)
    if not ir.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot place each anchor"
    var rr as result of bool to js.JsError is calling dom.remove with template
    if not rr.is_ok:
        calling panic with "tela: cannot detach each template"
    var ef as Effect is calling effect with (tpl_run of T), transmute st to ref to void
    return calling make_sub with ef.id, (free_tpl_state of T), transmute st to ref to void

weave free_tpl_config shard T with ctx as ref to void into void:
    var cfg as ref to TplConfig of T is transmute ctx to ref to TplConfig of T
    banish cfg

## Registra un binder para `data-tela-each`. La plantilla se clona por fila.
weave register_each shard T with key_fn as (weave with item as ref to T into string), bind_fn as (weave with item as ref to T, node as Elem into void), name as string, source as Signal of list of T into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if calling r->each_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: duplicate each name: " + name
    var cfg as ref to TplConfig of T is calling memoria.alloc of TplConfig of T
    set cfg->source is source.cell
    set cfg->key_fn is key_fn
    set cfg->bind_fn is bind_fn
    var e as EachEntry is with run is (tpl_start of T), free is (free_tpl_config of T), ctx is transmute cfg to ref to void
    calling r->each_entries.put with name, e

weave mount_each with node as dom.Element, name as string into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->each_entries.contains with name:
        calling panic with "tela: unknown each binder: " + name
    var e as EachEntry is calling r->each_entries.get with name
    var pr as result of maybe dom.Element to js.JsError is calling dom.parent with node
    if not pr.is_ok or pr.value is not present:
        calling panic with "tela: data-tela-each node has no parent"
    var parent as dom.Element is pr.value.value
    var sub as Subscription is calling e.run with e.ctx, parent, node
    calling dom.free with (sigil of parent)
    calling mount_add with sub

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- scopes

## Crea un scope vacío.
weave scope into Scope:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    var id as u64 is calling next_id
    var b as ref to ScopeBox is calling memoria.alloc of ScopeBox
    set b->subs is list of Subscription
    calling r->scopes.put with id, b
    return with id is id

## Añade una suscripción al scope; se libera con `scope_dispose`.
weave scope_add with sc as Scope, sub as Subscription into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->scopes.contains with sc.id:
        calling panic with "tela: disposed scope"
    var b as ref to ScopeBox is calling r->scopes.get with sc.id
    calling b->subs.push with sub

## Registra una limpieza sin efecto reactivo.
weave on_cleanup with sc as Scope, fn as (weave with ctx as ref to void into void), ctx as ref to void into void:
    calling scope_add with sc, (calling make_sub with 0, fn, ctx)

## Libera todas las suscripciones del scope.
weave scope_dispose with sc as Scope into void:
    var r as ref to Runtime is calling rt
    if not calling r->scopes.contains with sc.id:
        return
    var b as ref to ScopeBox is calling r->scopes.get with sc.id
    for sub in b->subs:
        calling sub.dispose
    calling b->subs.clear
    calling r->scopes.remove with sc.id
    banish b

## Async state holder: `data`, `loading`, `error` plus a version token.
##
## `resource` does not perform I/O. Call `begin` before a request, then
## `finish`/`fail` with the returned token from the callback. A stale response
## (different token) is ignored.
rune Resource shard T:
    data as Signal of maybe T
    loading as Signal of bool
    error as Signal of maybe string
    version as u64
    handle as maybe js.FetchHandle

weave resource shard T with initial as maybe T into Resource of T:
    var d as Signal of maybe T is calling signal with initial
    var l as Signal of bool is calling signal with false
    var en as maybe string is (maybe none)
    var e as Signal of maybe string is calling signal with en
    return with data is d, loading is l, error is e, version is 0, handle is (maybe none)

## Aborta el handle actual, si existe, y lo olvida.
weave abort_handle with h as maybe js.FetchHandle into void:
    if h is present:
        var br as result of bool to js.JsError is calling js.abort_request with h.value
        if br.is_ok:
            var ignored as bool is br.value

## Starts a load and returns its token. Aborta la petición anterior, marca
## loading y limpia el error.
weave begin shard T with r as ref to Resource of T into u64:
    calling abort_handle with r->handle
    set r->handle is maybe none
    set r->version is r->version + 1
    calling r->loading.set with true
    var en as maybe string is (maybe none)
    calling r->error.set with en
    return r->version

## Asocia el handle de la petición en curso. Si había otro, lo aborta.
weave attach_request shard T with r as (ref to Resource of T), h as js.FetchHandle into void:
    calling abort_handle with r->handle
    set r->handle is some h

## Cancela la petición en curso sin marcarla como error.
weave cancel shard T with r as ref to Resource of T into void:
    calling abort_handle with r->handle
    set r->handle is maybe none
    set r->version is r->version + 1
    calling r->loading.set with false
    var en as maybe string is (maybe none)
    calling r->error.set with en

## Applies a successful response only if `token` is still current.
weave finish shard T with r as (ref to Resource of T), token as u64, value as T into bool:
    if token == r->version:
        set r->handle is maybe none
        calling r->data.set with (some value)
        calling r->loading.set with false
        return true
    return false

## Applies an error only if `token` is still current.
weave fail shard T with r as (ref to Resource of T), token as u64, message as string into bool:
    if token == r->version:
        set r->handle is maybe none
        calling r->error.set with (some message)
        calling r->loading.set with false
        return true
    return false

weave dispose_resource shard T with r as (ref to Resource of T) into void:
    calling abort_handle with r->handle
    set r->handle is maybe none
    calling r->data.dispose
    calling r->loading.dispose
    calling r->error.dispose
    banish r
